{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HazyResearch/ncm/pulls/4","id":4904349518,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVEYivs8AAAABJFJvTg","html_url":"https://github.com/HazyResearch/ncm/pull/4","diff_url":"https://github.com/HazyResearch/ncm/pull/4.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/HazyResearch/ncm/pull/4.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HazyResearch/ncm/issues/4","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HazyResearch/ncm/pulls/4/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HazyResearch/ncm/pulls/4/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HazyResearch/ncm/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HazyResearch/ncm/issues/4/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HazyResearch/ncm/statuses/766e7d0043d439174e70cebd10c92d49b4b69d55","number":4,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":" Fix memory leak in generate(): read raw_token_prefix/contextual_prefix once","user":{"login":"velaia","id":1515904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTU5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1515904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/velaia","html_url":"https://github.com/velaia","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/velaia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/velaia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/velaia/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/velaia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/velaia/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/velaia/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/velaia/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/velaia/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/velaia/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"### Symptom\n\n`generate()` keeps all of its tensors alive after returning, until Python's cyclic garbage collector happens to run. That's effectively a memory leak between GC passes, and it roughly doubles peak memory. On an RTX 4090, peak memory of the eager path (1,024 sequences, fp32):\n\n| Task | Batch | Peak before | Peak after |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| XSum | 16 | 2.11 GB | 1.19 GB |\n| XSum | 64 | 5.82 GB | 2.52 GB |\n| WMT14 | 16 | 2.14 GB | 1.77 GB |\n| WMT14 | 64 | 5.04 GB | 3.66 GB |\n\nOutputs and wall-clock time are unchanged. With a KV cache (I'll send that in a separate PR), each leaked call also keeps the prefix K/V alive. That came to about 1.26 GB per XSum batch of 16, and XSum at batch 64 ran out of memory on the 24 GB card.\n\n### Cause\n\n`generate()` reads two optional flags from the model config on every call:\n\n```python\nif bool(getattr(self.config, 'raw_token_prefix', False)):\n    ...\n    if bool(getattr(self.config, 'contextual_prefix', False)) and \\\n```\n\nNone of the configs in `config/eval/` set `contextual_prefix`. For a missing key, `DictConfig.__getattr__` raises a `ConfigAttributeError`, and `getattr` catches it to return the default. Inside omegaconf, that exception and its traceback form a reference cycle that includes `generate()`'s frame. The frame therefore outlives the call, and so does every tensor it references, until the cyclic GC collects it. Minimal demo (omegaconf 2.3):\n\n```python\nimport gc, weakref\nfrom omegaconf import OmegaConf\nc = OmegaConf.create({'a': 1})\nclass T: pass\ndef f(key):\n    t = T(); r = weakref.ref(t)\n    getattr(c, key, None)\n    return r\ngc.disable()\nprint(f('a')() is None)  # True: freed on return\nprint(f('b')() is None)  # False: missing key, the local outlives the call\ngc.collect()             # now it is freed\n```\n\n### Fix\n\nRead both flags once in `__init__` and use the attributes in `generate()`. I checked the other `getattr(config, ..., default)` calls. All of them run once, in `__init__` or in the per-device cached flex block mask, so I left them alone.\n\n### Repro\n\nXSum checkpoint, batch 16, `top_k=1`, `gc.disable()`, memory allocated after each `generate()` call relative to before the first one. Apple M1 Max (MPS):\n\n| | call 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | after `gc.collect()` |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| before | +95 MB | +190 MB | +285 MB | +380 MB | +476 MB | +0 MB |\n| after | +0 MB | +0 MB | +0 MB | +0 MB | +0 MB | +0 MB |\n\nOn CPU with the unmodified repo (batch 4, bytes held by live tensors): +27 MB per call before, flat after.\n\nWMT14 (`evaluate.py --n 256`, MPS) produces identical outputs before and after: BLEU 17.84 / 18.59 lowercased.\n\n<sub>Note: upstream doesn't run on MPS yet. For the MPS numbers I applied a small local patch (device selection and an MPS-safe replacement for area interpolation) that isn't part of this PR.</sub>\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-17T22:11:14Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T22:11:14Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"8b44a0b90a8a4b052b63da83684a1ce17c2f4f65","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"velaia:fix-generate-config-leak","ref":"fix-generate-config-leak","repo":{"id":1421344717,"node_id":"R_kgDOVLf_zQ","name":"ncm","full_name":"velaia/ncm","owner":{"login":"velaia","id":1515904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTU5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1515904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/velaia","html_url":"https://github.com/velaia","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/velaia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/velaia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/velaia/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/velaia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/velaia/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/velaia/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/velaia/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/velaia/even